comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T10:26:49.672Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status corpus and fresh input_required task Windows search plus active/open lists found no active exact owner. Live full reads distinguish the closed pm-tm6h9x cleanup-coverage fix from this Windows input/failure wait. Preserve the original hosted failure; this is a new scoped recurrence under the existing flake-detection lineage, not a reopened or duplicated completed implementation."
  "2026-10-24T10:31:05.239Z","harness:codex","Independent negative control: in a detached temporary checkout, delayed only the mocked task operation by1000ms while preserving real task storage and protocol calls. The unchanged100-attempt/five-ms helper fails with task did not reach input_required. The root test now retains that representative slow operation and uses a10-second elapsed-time condition wait with25ms intervals for the official tasks/get protocol. All input-required, resume, stable completion and protocol error assertions remain; no production export, skip, quarantine or test-timeout ceiling was added. Hosted Windows acceptance is still required."
  "2026-10-24T10:32:58.513Z","harness:codex","Positive control: the same representative1000ms task delay that defeated the original attempt-count helper passes under the bounded elapsed-time wait. The complete9-case MCP branch suite passes with all existing eligibility, input, resume, stable completion, protocol-failure and persistence-error controls retained. No production task implementation was changed. A fresh hosted Windows matrix will verify the platform-specific recurrence."
